/node_modules
/.next
/out
/build
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*

# Cloudflare (OpenNext)
/.open-next
/.wrangler
cloudflare-env.d.ts

# Secrets.
#
# Deny by name, then re-admit the two example files, because the old list named only the
# exact files that existed (.env, .env*.local, .dev.vars) and let every neighbouring
# spelling through: .env.production, .dev.vars.local and .dev.vars.production were all
# committable. On a public repo one such file is the whole Google OAuth client, so the
# default has to be "ignored" and the exception has to be spelled out.
.env*
!.env.example
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example

# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at build time, so a build-time env file (.env.production) is the
# one that may legitimately need committing. It stays ignored here: commit it with
# `git add -f` after reading it, and never put a server secret in it.

# Credential files, which arrive already named by whoever exported them.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*client_secret*.json
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
